11.2 Coordinate reference systems
All routines in spatstat are layed out for two-dimensional data with Cartesian coordinates. If we try to convert an object with ellipsoidal coordinates, we get an error:

system.file("gpkg/nc.gpkg", package = "sf") |&gt; 
    read_sf() |&gt;
    st_geometry() |&gt;
    st_centroid() |&gt;
    as.ppp()
# Error:
# ! Only projected coordinates may be converted to spatstat
# class objects

When converting to a spatstat data structure we lose the coordinate reference system we started with. It can be set back to sf or stars objects by using st_set_crs.
